meta {
  name: SiteAdmin List Audits
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/siteadmin/audits?page=1&limit=20
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 20
  ~tenantId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  ~module: BRANCH
  ~action: CREATE
  ~search: branch
  ~actorPersonId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  ~branchId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  ~from: 2026-06-01
  ~to: 2026-06-30
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{siteAdminToken}}
}

docs {
  SiteAdmin audit view: a MERGED, paginated audit trail combining two sources,
  newest first — business `audit_logs` across ALL businesses (or a single one via
  `tenantId`) AND platform-level SiteAdmin actions (`siteadmin_audit_logs`).
  Pagination info (`total / page / limit / totalPages`) is lifted into `meta`.

  Auth: SiteAdmin token, permission `audit-logs:read` (operations_admin and above).

  All query params are optional (the `~`-prefixed ones above are disabled
  examples — enable the ones you need):

  - `page` (>=1, default 1) / `limit` (1-100, default 20) — pagination.
  - `tenantId` — restrict to a single business/tenant (omit for all businesses).
    NOTE: when set, SiteAdmin (tenant-less) rows are excluded.
  - `module` — filter by functional area. Business examples: `USER`, `BRANCH`,
    `SCHEDULE`, `TENANT`, `AUTH`. SiteAdmin examples: `SITEADMIN`, `EQUIPMENT`,
    `CONTACT_US`, `SUPPORT_INFO`, `AUTH_ROLE`, `TEST_GROUP`, `PAYMENT_RULE`,
    `LOCATION`, `TEMPLATE`, `PDF_REPORT_TEMPLATE`.
  - `action` — filter by operation. One of:
    `CREATE`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `LOGIN`, `LOGOUT`, `EXPORT`, `OTHER`.
  - `actorPersonId` — exact person id of the actor (business rows only; setting
    this excludes SiteAdmin rows).
  - `branchId` — exact branch id (branch-level business events; setting this
    excludes SiteAdmin rows).
  - `from` / `to` — inclusive `createdAt` bounds (ISO-8601 date or datetime).
  - `search` — case-insensitive substring matched against the actor
    (person id / role label / SiteAdmin email) and the description.

  Each item carries a `scope` discriminator: `'TENANT'` or `'SITEADMIN'`.
  Common audit fields on every row: `createdAt`, `module`, `action`,
  `description`, `ipAddress`, `actorPersonId` (for SiteAdmin rows this is the
  SiteAdmin id), `actorRoleKey`, `actorRoleLabel`, `resourceId`, `metadata`,
  plus enrichment `actorName`, `actorUsername`.
  - TENANT rows: `tenantId`/`tenantName` set (business name); `branchId` may be set;
    `actorName`/`actorUsername` are the person's name + system username.
  - SITEADMIN rows: `tenantId`/`tenantName`/`branchId` are `null`;
    `actorName`/`actorUsername` are the SiteAdmin email and `actorRoleLabel` the role.
}
